{"kind":"request","text":"Operator-directed (2026-08-28; operator sanctioned filing findings 1-3 from checker's comprehensive tailapps review; this is priority 1 of 3). Fix the MCP tools/call reply envelope for array-shaped results. internal/mcp/server.go:89 attaches structuredContent set to the raw engine result on every tools/call reply. The apps_list operation returns a top-level JSON array, but MCP requires structuredContent to be a JSON object, so Claude Code 2.1.251 rejects the tailapps_list reply client-side with 'MCP server \"tailapp\" returned a malformed result that failed schema validation: Invalid result for tools/call: ... expected record, received array' even though the server-side call succeeds. tailapp_status and tailapp_metrics (the other parameterless tools) are unaffected because their results are objects. Verified live this session against the running serve, sources at local main 87a7c44b1816620e9947c33e2cad4d3c9e0ee9ca. Recommended fix: either omit structuredContent when the marshaled result is not a JSON object (structuredContent is optional per the MCP spec, and the text content block already carries the full JSON), or wrap array results in a stable object shape such as {\"apps\": [...]} - note wrapping changes the tool's output contract for existing clients, so choose deliberately and document the choice. Add a regression test that drives an array-returning operation through the reply path. This is distinct from the properties:null tools/list bug fixed under #724.","body":{"conditions":"Fix in internal/mcp with a regression test covering an array-shaped tools/call result; full battery green; an effective checker review verdict at the exact implementation head.","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}